# Copy to the target project root as `.gitignore`.
# Public-repo baseline: keep ALL credentials and context docs out of git.

# --- Secrets & private context (NEVER commit) ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
CLAUDE.md
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
# native Firebase credentials
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist
# backend service-account JSON (any name)
*service-account*.json
firebase-*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json

# --- Dependencies / build output ---
node_modules/
dist/
build/
target/
.expo/
web-build/
*.log

# --- Tooling ---
.codegraph/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
coverage/

# Notes:
# - `.env.example` is the ONLY env file tracked; it holds placeholders only.
# - CLAUDE.md / IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md are gitignored because they hold config + test creds.
#   The tracked agent note is AGENTS.md (no secrets).
# - Backend (Quarkus): also ignore src/main/resources/firebase-*.json and any local .env.
